The following commands and their implementations are based on patterns and concepts
from Kubernetes kubectl and OpenShift CLI:
- get, create, edit, delete, describe, logs, apply, patch (kubectl-like commands)
- annotate, label (resource annotation and labeling)
- Table printing formats and column layouts for resource display (matching kubectl/oc output)
- All resource management operations follow kubectl patterns and conventions

**Diagnostics:**
The diagnostics command suite provides health check capabilities for cluster components,
leveraging SSH access for deep inspection of node metrics and services.

**Table Printing:**
Table output formats for the following resources are designed to match kubectl/oc behavior:
- Pods, Deployments, ReplicaSets, StatefulSets, DaemonSets
- Jobs, CronJobs
- Services, Secrets, ConfigMaps, ServiceAccounts
- Nodes, Namespaces
- Machine Config Pools (OpenShift)
- Routes (OpenShift)
- Wide output (-owide) implementations following kubectl patterns

This product includes support for OpenShift-specific Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs)
and resources, including but not limited to:
- Routes (route.openshift.io/v1)
- BuildConfigs and Builds (build.openshift.io/v1)
- DeploymentConfigs (apps.openshift.io/v1)
- ImageStreams, ImageStreamTags, ImageStreamImages (image.openshift.io/v1)
- Templates (template.openshift.io/v1)
- Projects (project.openshift.io/v1)
- ClusterResourceQuotas (quota.openshift.io/v1)
- SecurityContextConstraints (security.openshift.io/v1)
- NetworkAttachmentDefinitions (k8s.cni.cncf.io/v1)
- ClusterOperators and ClusterVersions (config.openshift.io/v1)
- MachineConfigPools (machineconfiguration.openshift.io/v1)

All OpenShift resources are accessed via the Kubernetes dynamic client API and follow
the same patterns and concepts as the OpenShift CLI (oc).

This product uses the following third-party libraries:

- Kubernetes client-go (k8s.io/client-go)
- Kubernetes API (k8s.io/api)
- Kubernetes apimachinery (k8s.io/apimachinery)
- sigs.k8s.io/yaml
- github.com/spf13/cobra (CLI framework)

