**Resource Discovery:**
This product uses the Kubernetes API server discovery mechanism to dynamically discover
all available resources (including Custom Resource Definitions/CRDs) in the cluster.
This allows the CLI to work with any Kubernetes distribution and any custom resources
without hardcoding resource types. The discovery client (k8s.io/client-go/discovery)
is used to query the API server for available API groups, versions, and resources.

**Resource Aliases and Shortcuts:**
The CLI provides comprehensive aliases and shortcuts for common resources to improve
usability. For example, users can use `ocp get mcp` instead of `ocp get machineconfigpools`,
or `ocp get crd` instead of `ocp get customresourcedefinitions`. All standard Kubernetes
and OpenShift resource shortcuts are supported (e.g., `po` for pods, `svc` for services,
`deploy` for deployments, `co` for clusteroperators, `cv` for clusterversions, etc.).
These aliases are automatically resolved during resource discovery.

**clearyml Command:**
The clearyml command implementation follows kubectl/oc patterns for resource retrieval
and YAML output, but includes custom logic for cleaning/sanitizing YAML output by
removing status fields, managed fields, resource versions, and other runtime-generated
metadata. This makes the output suitable for version control and re-application to clusters.
